{
  "dom_id": "step-q19160",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the following table of values for $f(x).$ Knowing that the average rate of change of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-2,3]$ is $3,$ find the value of $p.$ \n\n| $x$ | $\\,-5\\,$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,5\\,$ | $\\,7\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,-11\\,$ | $\\,2p-1\\,$ | $\\,-5\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ | $\\,p+10\\,$ | $\\,7\\,$ | $\\,8\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3)-f(-2)}{3-(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(p+10)-(2p-1)}{3+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11-p}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we know that $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=3$ on the interval $[-2,3].$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\frac{11-p}{5}=3.\n$$\n\nSolving for $p,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11-p}{5} & =3 \\\\ 11-p & =15 \\\\ -p & =15-11 \\\\ -p & =4 \\\\ p & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "selection",
      "type": "radio",
